          "Calendars",
          "should not",
          "run your day.",
          "You should."
        ],
        "paragraphs": [
          "Most scheduling tools were built to record what already happened. They log visits well, yet they rarely help a dispatcher decide what to move next, and that gap fills every morning with phone calls.",
          "We would rather give dispatch a proper control room. Maps, crews, parts and customer notes sit side by side, arranged the way a coordinator reads them, so each decision takes seconds instead of minutes.",
          "A room like that remembers every promise, flags the visit that will run late, and keeps the whole team moving at one pace.",
          "Local knowledge, tough judgment calls and the handshake at the door still belong to your people. This is only a better desk to work from."
        ],
